# Version bump on ship

Every shipped change (commit/push to `master`, or a user-facing release) must increment the version. The in-app updater compares version numbers, not commits.

- Patch `0.1.x` for fixes and small behavior changes
- Minor `0.x.0` for new features
- Keep these in lockstep: `pyproject.toml` `version`, `src/ludo/__init__.py` `__version__`, and `packaging/arch/PKGBUILD` (`pkgver` and `pkgver()`)
- Include the bump in the same commit as the change when possible
- Do not ship code on `master` with the previous version still set
